        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(protocol): pre-publish cheat-window cleanup and vintage tracking",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWe are preparing `@openclaw/gateway-protocol` for public npm publication. Before the surface freezes into public API, this PR executes the \"cheat window\" cleanup: hard reshapes of protocol families that are provably unshipped (no release tag and/or no shipped store-binary callers), deletion of dead public surface, and durable release-train vintage tracking so future \"what shipped when\" questions are answerable mechanically.\n\nShipped-surface audit backing the window (verified against tags + store builds): the `question.*` family is in no release tag; the worker stack / session catalog / durable approvals families are `v2026.7.2-beta` only; native store apps call none of the reshaped families (their \"terminal\" is a WebView, not RPCs). `tts.speak` and `agents.workspace.*` have shipped iOS/Android callers and are untouched.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- `question.*`: `id` meant two different things (per-question id and request-record id) and the answers map double-nested (`Record<id, { answers: string[] }>`). Renamed per-question id to `questionId`, flattened answers to `Record<questionId, string[]>`, moved the 12-cap header enforcement to the gateway (TypeBox grapheme semantics) with clamp-not-reject at tool and UI boundaries, and guarded prototype-key ids (`constructor`) in resolve validation.\n- Worker stack: converted ~120 lines of handwritten type mirrors to `Static<>`, extracted duplicated primitives into `worker-protocol-primitives.ts`, un-exported/deleted unconsumed schemas, kept placement variants required by generated Swift.\n- Session catalog: one shared `SessionCatalogLocator`, `openClawSessionKey` -> `sessionKey`, flattened `SessionsCatalogListParams` (removing the Swift generator merged-union carve-out).\n- Dead surface: deleted 55 unused outbound validators plus ~80 zero-consumer schemas/types (verified against consumers, the ProtocolSchemas registry, and generated Swift/Kotlin), added `\"sideEffects\": false` + pure annotation so consumers can tree-shake, replaced `HealthSnapshotSchema = Type.Any()` with a producer-shaped closed schema, annotated deprecated compat fields.\n- Vintage: `since` metadata on all 309 core method specs (precise `2026.7` for this train's families, `<=2026.7` sentinel backfill), `x-openclaw-since` schema annotations, a merge-base-diff guard script wired into `protocol:check`, and a completeness test.\n- Rode along: fixed a latent codex side-thread race (late dynamic-tool handlers publishing diagnostics after cleanup) that the reshape made deterministic.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo impact on shipped stable users or store apps: reshaped families have no shipped callers. Beta users of `v2026.7.2-beta.*` worker/catalog surfaces see the new shapes on next beta (breakage explicitly accepted by maintainer). Control UI ships lockstep with the gateway. External consumers gain a smaller, tree-shakeable, honestly-documented protocol surface ahead of npm publication.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused suites green per stage (questions/gateway/harness/ask-user/UI; worker 572 tests + catalog 711 tests on Blacksmith Testbox run 29661844234; gateway-protocol package suite 245 tests; health snapshot suite; since guard + descriptor ordering tests post-rebase).\n- Generation stability proven per stage: protocol-gen + Swift + Kotlin run twice with identical diffs; generated models byte-identical for the vintage commit.\n- Autoreview per stage until convergence; two real findings fixed (prototype-chain lookup with regression test; header Unicode-semantics clamp), compat-window findings consciously rejected with the shipped-surface audit above. Post-rebase commits reviewed clean in commit mode. Note: full-branch bundle mode trips the reviewer's secret-fragment scanner on pre-existing test fixtures; per-commit coverage is complete.\n- Net diff: strongly LOC-negative (worker/catalog −161, dead surface −614 non-test lines).\n",
        "branch": "claude/protocol-cheat-cleanup",
